WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.994
Content type names, field names, custom admin menu items and some permission descriptions

00:00:06.994 --> 00:00:13.177
depend on your site's data, so PO files, the usual translation files, cannot translate them.

00:00:13.177 --> 00:00:16.269
Data Localization does, culture by culture.

00:00:16.269 --> 00:00:20.370
We'll enable it, translate into French, and see the result.

00:00:24.970 --> 00:00:28.230
PO files translate the fixed text of the interface.

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:31.089
Other text depends on the data of your site:

00:00:31.089 --> 00:00:33.377
names that you or a module create.

00:00:33.377 --> 00:00:35.150
These are the main kinds.

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:40.987
The Data Localization feature stores translations in the database, one set for each

00:00:40.987 --> 00:00:43.216
culture, such as French (France).

00:00:43.216 --> 00:00:47.274
A page that shows one of these names looks up the translation for

00:00:47.274 --> 00:00:49.161
the culture of the request.

00:00:49.161 --> 00:00:51.790
Without one, it shows the original text.

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:54.884
Each kind of text has its own tool.

00:00:54.884 --> 00:01:00.316
PO files translate the fixed interface, Data Localization translates names that come from

00:01:00.316 --> 00:01:06.320
your site's data, and Content Localization translates content items, which a separate video covers.

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:14.363
Data Localization depends on the Localization feature.

00:01:14.363 --> 00:01:19.041
On this site, Localization is enabled, with three supported cultures:

00:01:19.041 --> 00:01:21.162
English, French and Spanish.

00:01:21.162 --> 00:01:23.220
Let's open Tools, Features.

00:01:23.673 --> 00:01:25.841
Let's search for Data Localization.

00:01:25.841 --> 00:01:28.432
It is in the Internationalization category.

00:01:28.432 --> 00:01:32.293
Select Enable, and a message confirms that the feature was enabled.

00:01:32.756 --> 00:01:39.936
The feature adds Dynamic Translations to the admin menu, under Settings, Localization, next to Cultures.

00:01:44.183 --> 00:01:46.186
Select Dynamic Translations.

00:01:46.186 --> 00:01:51.196
The Culture drop-down lists the supported cultures, and the editor opens on the

00:01:51.196 --> 00:01:53.613
first one, English (United States).

00:01:54.097 --> 00:01:56.156
Let's choose French (France).

00:01:56.156 --> 00:01:58.744
The strings are grouped in categories:

00:01:58.744 --> 00:02:02.567
Admin Menus, Content Fields, Content Types and Permissions.

00:02:03.038 --> 00:02:07.698
Beside each category name, the editor shows how many strings it holds, and

00:02:07.698 --> 00:02:09.446
how many are translated.

00:02:09.446 --> 00:02:13.698
Each row pairs the original text with an input for its translation.

00:02:14.184 --> 00:02:17.390
The Category drop-down shows one category at a time.

00:02:17.390 --> 00:02:22.311
Search filters the strings by their original text or their translation, and Missing

00:02:22.311 --> 00:02:25.684
only hides the strings that already have a translation.

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:32.483
Let's translate a content type name.

00:02:32.483 --> 00:02:36.466
Set the category to Content Types, and search for Blog Post.

00:02:36.466 --> 00:02:40.389
This type has no French translation, so its input is empty.

00:02:40.908 --> 00:02:42.398
Type Article de blog.

00:02:42.398 --> 00:02:47.256
Auto-save stores it two seconds after you stop typing, and Save stores it at once.

00:02:47.256 --> 00:02:50.458
A message confirms that the translations were saved.

00:02:51.072 --> 00:02:53.054
Field names work the same way.

00:02:53.054 --> 00:02:58.174
Under Content Fields, the strings are grouped by the content part that holds the field.

00:02:58.174 --> 00:03:01.752
Let's translate Tags, in the BlogPost group, as Étiquettes.

00:03:02.243 --> 00:03:07.403
In Admin Menus, the top-level items of the admin menus you build are listed too.

00:03:07.403 --> 00:03:10.403
Let's translate Main Menu as Menu principal.

00:03:10.403 --> 00:03:14.123
A saved translation applies without restarting the site.

00:03:18.318 --> 00:03:22.105
To see the result, switch the admin to French with the culture picker

00:03:22.105 --> 00:03:25.639
in the top bar, which the Admin Culture Picker feature provides.

00:03:25.639 --> 00:03:27.507
Let's choose français (France).

00:03:27.507 --> 00:03:29.578
A separate video covers the picker.

00:03:30.034 --> 00:03:31.347
The page reloads.

00:03:31.347 --> 00:03:35.003
The admin menu lists Menu principal in place of Main Menu.

00:03:35.003 --> 00:03:39.058
The rest of the interface stays in English, since no PO files are

00:03:39.058 --> 00:03:40.714
installed on this site.

00:03:41.175 --> 00:03:45.693
On Manage Content, the New menu lists the content types that are set

00:03:45.693 --> 00:03:49.539
as Creatable, with Article de blog in place of Blog Post.

00:03:49.539 --> 00:03:54.545
The admin translates content type names in its lists, menus and page titles.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:59.022
Choose Article de blog, and the title reads New Article de blog.

00:03:59.022 --> 00:04:03.160
Further down, the field that was named Tags is labeled Étiquettes.

00:04:07.346 --> 00:04:09.803
In the editor, select Statistics.

00:04:09.803 --> 00:04:16.606
Overall Progress compares the translated strings with all the strings, across every supported culture.

00:04:17.072 --> 00:04:21.658
Progress by Culture shows a bar and a count for each culture.

00:04:21.658 --> 00:04:27.202
A bar is green from 75 percent, yellow from 25 percent, and red below that.

00:04:27.693 --> 00:04:30.844
Progress by Category breaks one culture down.

00:04:30.844 --> 00:04:36.713
Choose a culture in the Culture drop-down, and each category shows its own bar and count.

00:04:40.913 --> 00:04:44.159
You grant these permissions on the role editor.

00:04:44.159 --> 00:04:51.326
Manage all dynamic translations edits every culture, and View dynamic translations and statistics is read-only.

00:04:51.326 --> 00:04:57.573
Each supported culture also has its own permission, such as Manage French (France) translations.

00:04:58.323 --> 00:05:04.123
By default, the Administrator role manages all translations, and the Editor role can view them.

00:05:04.123 --> 00:05:09.463
A user who can only view sees the editor with a read-only message, and disabled inputs.

00:05:13.663 --> 00:05:18.971
To move translations to another site, add the Translations step to a deployment plan.

00:05:18.971 --> 00:05:22.237
It exports the cultures and categories you choose.

00:05:22.237 --> 00:05:26.553
Then import the result on a site where Data Localization is enabled.

00:05:28.553 --> 00:05:30.115
That's Data Localization:

00:05:30.115 --> 00:05:34.297
translations for the names that come from your site's data, edited culture by

00:05:34.297 --> 00:05:36.413
culture and tracked with statistics.

00:05:36.413 --> 00:05:37.723
Thanks for watching.

